{
  "text": " Joe Biden says the pandemic is over, so why are teachers still being fired for not being vaccinated? Is the pandemic over? The pandemic is over, we still have a problem with Covid, we're still doing a lot of work on it. It's what the pandemic is over. Okay, so there we have it, the pandemic is over, cause for optimism, cause for joy and celebration. Finally some good news we can get behind. But during the point of the pandemic that most people were concerned to some degree or another about the outcomes, the impact financially, medically, socially, etc. Do you know who we were invited to take into our hearts as heroes? Quite rightly in my view, nurses, teachers, people in services, people that simply had to continue working because their duty and their job demanded it. Why then if the pandemic is over, is this happening? Well in New York City nearly 2,000 school staffers are out of a job for not complying with the Covid vaccine mandate. According to the New York Post, the Department of Education has fired another 850 teachers and classroom aides after they failed to get the shot. That mandate was opposed by former Mayor Bill de Blasio last October. The DOE told the Post that teachers agreed to show proof of vaccination by September or be considered quote to have voluntarily resigned. The New York City Department of Education has asked another 850 teachers and classroom aides, bringing the total to nearly 2,000 school employees fired for failure to comply with the vaccine mandate. About 1,300 DOE employees who took a year's unpaid leave, so essentially they were sacked anyway, unpaid leave with benefits, agreed to show proof of Covid vaccination by September the 5th or be deemed to have voluntarily resigned. That's like stop hitting yourself, isn't it? That's like bullying. Stop hitting yourself, stop hitting, why are you resigning for? Why are you not getting vaccinated for? Why are you resigning for? Rachelle Garcia, an elementary school teacher in Brooklyn for 15 years and mother of two, worked fully in person during the pandemic and never got sick, she said, but she refused to get vaccinated, finally taking leave after the DOE denied her request for a religious exemption.",
